<title>NETHERLANDS: WOLTERS KLUWER 1996 NET NLG 479 MLN.</title>
<headline>WOLTERS KLUWER 1996 NET NLG 479 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)		     7.03  vs    6.70</p>
<p>    Net profit				   479     vs  452</p>
<p>    Sales (billions)			     4.32  vs    2.94</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected law and tax publisher Wolters</p>
<p>Kluwer to report a 1996 net profit of 461-491 million guilders</p>
<p>with the consensus forecast at 480 million.</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)			  2.48  vs    2.16</p>
<p>    Operating costs (billions)		 3.39  vs    2.34</p>
<p>Operating income before</p>
<p>    amortisation of goodwill		 927     vs  609</p>
<p>    Amortisation of goodwill		  65     vs  nil</p>
<p>    Interest charges			   164     vs    6 gain</p>
<p>    Taxes					  215     vs  174</p>
<p>    Extraordinary charges			4     vs   11 gain</p>
<p>WOLTER KLUWER COSTS IN DETAIL</p>
<p>    Materials/external costs (billions)    2.03  vs    1.54</p>
<p>    Personnel (billion)			  1.24  vs    0.74</p>
<p>    Depreciation				 113     vs   59</p>
<p>    Total operating costs (billions)	 3.39  vs    2.34</p>
<p>NOTE - Wolters Kluwer said the 1996 dividend could be taken</p>
<p>up either in cash or as an optional payment in new shares, the</p>
<p>details of which will be published on April 17.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
